[8381]="Armaments of War\031\031\031War comes, $N, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.$B$BShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...$B$B<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>$B$BThe future of us all could be at an end.$B$BThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.",
[8382]="Armaments of War\031\031\031War comes, $N, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.$B$BShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...$B$B<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>$B$BThe future of us all could be at an end.$B$BThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.",
[8383]="Remember Alterac Valley!\031The Battle in Alterac Valley rages on, $N! Have you done your part as of late, $N?\031Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\031You continue to honor the Alliance, $N. The Horde will be crushed before long if we keep our efforts up.",
[8384]="OLD Claiming Arathi Basin\031Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.$B$BWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.$B$BIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, $N.\031Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.",
[8385]="Concerted Efforts\031Ah, $N. I hope you continue to lend your experience to the different battlefronts. A lot of our lads and lasses in the field look up to seasoned veterans like you.\031\031You live up to yer reputation, $N. Without people like you, the Alliance wouldn't stand a chance against the savage forces of the Horde.\031Ah, $N. I hope you continue to lend your experience to the different battlefronts. A lot of our lads and lasses in the field look up to seasoned veterans like you.",
[8386]="OLD Fight for Warsong Gulch\031The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.$B$BThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.$B$BDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, $N! For the Alliance!\031Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\031Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\031Do you bear news from Warsong Gulch, $N?",
[8387]="Invaders of Alterac Valley\031The battle for Alterac rages on! You must return to Alterac Valley and once more drive the invaders out of Frostwolf territory, $N!\031Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\031Good work, $N! You should be proud of yourself. The Alliance invaders must be expelled from Alterac!\031What news do you bring from the lands of the Frostwolves?  How does the battle for Alterac Valley fare?",
[8388]="For Great Honor\031Many brave fighters look up to you, $N. You continue to be an example for all in the fight against the Alliance. What news do you bring from your journeys?\031\031You continue to honor the Horde, $N. I'm glad to see you haven't turned soft.\031Arathi is still wet with the blood of great warriors and the clash of steel still rings throughout Alterac. Do not waste my time unless you bring news from the front!",
[8389]="OLD Battle of Warsong Gulch\031The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.$B$BDo not let this happen, $N! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!\031Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\031Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\031The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.$B$BDo not let this happen, $N! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!",
[8390]="OLD Conquering Arathi Basin\031Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.$B$BThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, $N!\031Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.",
[8391]="OLD Claiming Arathi Basin\031Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.$B$BWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.$B$BIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, $N.\031Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.",
[8392]="OLD Claiming Arathi Basin\031Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.$B$BWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.$B$BIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, $N.\031Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.",
