[8727]="Farwhisper the Elder\031\031\031The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, $N. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?",
[8728]="The Good News and The Bad News\031Well that took a little longer than expected. Now let me see what this ledger says.$B$B<Narain silently reads the ledger, periodically mumbling under his breath.>$B$B The good news is that I am 99% certain that I am capable of creating an arcanite buoy that will function to your specifications. This is, of course, wholly dependant on the bad news.$B$BThe bad news is that I'm going to need a lot of arcanite, elementium ore, and rare gemstones.$B$BBring me what I need and I will craft the buoy.\031Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris wants you to bring him 20 Arcanite Bars, 10 Elementium Ore, 10 Azerothian Diamonds, and 10 Blue Sapphires.\031A deal is a deal. I sure hope you know what you are getting yourself into, $N. This is an awful lot of trouble to go through to do some fishing.\031Arcanite buoys don't just make themselves, $N. And NO, you cannot borrow some money.",
[8729]="The Wrath of Neptulon\031Did I mention the bad news yet? Its name is Maws: 100 feet of death and destruction. I guess I may have forgotten that little tidbit.$B$BAccording to my superior psycho-psionic clairvoyance, you'll find that the best spot to cast this buoy is off the coast of Azshara, in the Bay of Storms.$B$BLook for a swirling maelstrom, most likely cluttered with wreckage.$B$BBy the by, I hope you have friends.$B$BNow if you somehow miraculously succeed, take the scepter shard to Anachronos.\031Use the Arcanite Buoy at the Swirling Maelstrom at the Bay of Storms in Azshara.\031Well done, $N. I will be able to reform the Scepter of the Shifting Sands soon.\031Time is running out, champion.",
[8730]="Nefarius's Corruption\031Champion, is it you? A thousand years it has been since I was entrusted the shard and it is at my darkest hour that one should rise to relieve me of it... But what would tragedy be without cruelty?$B$B<Vaelastrasz coughs weakly.>$B$BNe... Nefarius now holds the scepter shard.$B$BTime is of the essence. Nefarius plans to destroy the shard. You must hurry!\031Slay Nefarian and recover the Red Scepter Shard. Return the Red Scepter Shard to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris. You have 5 hours to complete this task.\031Vaelastrasz's soul is at ease, champion. The Aspects all watch your progress with great interest. Know that you have powerful allies.$B$BI was commanded to grant you something to aid you in this struggle. Use it well...\031Another of our heroes lost to the spawn of Deathwing. We will be cursed with this suffering forever...",
[8731]="Field Duty\031Greetings, $N.  Before I assign you to more involved tasks in the war, you'll need to do your share of field duty.  $B$BYou will find Captain Skullsplit's Orgrimmar Legion outside Hive'Regal.$B$BReport to him and come back to me with proof of your field service.  I shall have a more advanced assignment ready for you.$B$BOh, please do your best to stay away from the Ironforge Brigade.  Tensions are high among our Alliance and Horde volunteers.\031Report to Krug Skullsplit at the Orgrimmar Legion post in front of Hive'Regal.  Prepare your Unsigned Field Duty Papers, obtain Signed Field Duty Papers and bring them to Windcaller Kaldon in Cenarion Hold.$B$BNote: Healing or casting beneficial spells on a member of the Orgrimmar Legion will flag you for PvP.\031I can tell that Krug has little use for paperwork. He signed this in silithid blood!$B$BVery well, $N. I've prepared a set of tasks that should make good use of your skills as a $c.$B$BWith the continued efforts of you and people like you, our enemy will soon be crushed!\031You've completed your field duty, $N?  Captain Skullsplit can be found outside of Hive'Regal.",
[8732]="Field Duty Papers\031\031\031Yes, I suppose that little skirmish will pass as field duty nowadays. Take these back to Cenarion Hold, I'm sure they'll have a cushy job ready for you.$B$BOff you go!\031I take it you want those papers signed, $Gboy:girl;?",
[8733]="Eranikus, Tyrant of the Dream\031This is a journey of redemption, hero. Would it be that I was slain today, I would have died for a just and righteous cause. You must recover the green scepter shard. You must cleanse Eranikus of the taint placed upon him by the Old Gods.$B$BTravel to Darnassus. Just outside the city walls you will find one of my agents. This agent will set things in motion for us and inform Tyrande of our plans without alerting Staghelm.$B$B<Malfurion sighs.>$B$BA fall from grace a thousand years in the making...\031Travel to the continent of Teldrassil and find Malfurion's agent somewhere outside the walls of Darnassus.\031The wisp is silent except for a low humming sound. Oddly enough, it is able to communicate with you through thoughts.",
[8734]="Tyrande and Remulos\031Tyrande will be notifed, mortal. Shan'do Stormrage has prepared me for this contingency.$B$BNow you must venture to the Moonglade and speak with Remulos. He will have further instruction as to the summoning of Eranikus.$B$BWe all wish you great luck.\031Travel to the Moonglade and speak to Keeper Remulos.\031It would be impossible to pull Eranikus from the Dream should he refuse. His intentions, however, require him to enter our world. He seeks to destroy the living manifestation of Malfurion. To do this successfully would mean an end to one of the most powerful allies of the Dream. The Nightmare would wholly consume all that would remain should Malfurion fall...",
[8735]="The Nightmare's Corruption\031You must travel to the four dream portals of Azeroth. From each you must draw a fragment of the Nightmare's corruption. The dragonkin that inhabit these areas will hold such fragments. Return to me when you have gathered these fragments.\031Travel to the four Emerald Dream portals in Azeroth and collect a Fragment of the Nightmare's Corruption from each. Return to Keeper Remulos in the Moonglade when you have completed this task.\031Are you prepared? Is the world prepared for what we are about to invoke? I do not know... I am bound by duty to Malfurion. Duty and honor...\031<Remulos is lost deep in thought.>",
[8736]="The Nightmare Manifests\031We must use restraint against Eranikus. We are to redeem him not destroy him.$B$BTyrande is already en route to assist us in this task. We must weather the dragon's blows and save Nighthaven from certain destruction.$B$BBe on guard! You and your allies are our only hope.\031Defend Nighthaven from Eranikus. Do not let Keeper Remulos perish. Do not slay Eranikus. Defend yourself. Await Tyrande.\031He is redeemed, $n. He now returns to the Dream to right what he alone has done wrong. Eranikus will be a powerful ally to Malfurion and my father.$b$bThese armaments are for you, $n; given to me by Ysera herself. You would do well to make use of them in your battles against the Qiraji.\031\031The Redemption of Eranikus",
[8737]="Azure Templar\031The Twilight's Hammer and the elemental nobles they worship present a formidable threat to our operations in Silithus.  With the new enemies we're facing inside Ahn'Qiraj, we cannot afford to lower our guard to our enemies outside.$B$BFind a way to summon and destroy an Azure Templar and report to Bor Wildmane.\031Summon and slay an Azure Templar and report back to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.  You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.\031Good job, $N. Here's your next assignment.\031Is your task done yet, $N?",
[8738]="Hive'Regal Scout Report\031We've sent our best scouts deep into the silithid hives to gather intelligence.  Scout Landion has been watching the silithid movements at Hive'Regal for several days now.  Find him and obtain a written report.  We need to be able to act on that information as soon as possible, $N.\031Contact Cenarion Scout Landion inside Hive'Regal and return the Hive'Regal Scout Report to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold.  You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing VII in order to complete this quest.\031Your efforts are greatly appreciated, $N. I'll read these scouting reports right away, feel free to go over your next assignment.\031You'll find Scout Landion inside Hive'regal. Hurry, $N! Time is of the essence.",
[8739]="Hive'Ashi Scout Report\031We've sent our best scouts deep into the silithid hives to gather intelligence.  Scout Jalia has been watching the silithid movements at Hive'Ashi for several days now.  Find her and obtain a written report.  We need to be able to act on that information as soon as possible, $N.\031Contact Cenarion Scout Jalia inside Hive'Ashi and return the Hive'Ashi Scout Report to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold.  You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.\031Your efforts are greatly appreciated, $N. I'll read these scouting reports right away, feel free to go over your next assignment.\031You'll find Scout Jalia inside Hive'Ashi.  Hurry, $N!  Time is of the essence.",
[8740]="Twilight Marauders\031Bands of mounted Twilight's Hammer cultists have been spotted riding outside the reach of our forces in Cenarion Hold, picking off our smaller patrols and caravans.$B$BFind and defeat the twilight marauders along with their leader, a terrible warrior by the name of Morna.  Report to Windcaller Proudhorn after completing the task.\031Slay Twilight Marauder Morna and 2 Twilight Marauders.  Report to Windcaller Proudhorn when your task is finished.  You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.\031Well done, $N. The twilight marauders were inflicting an unacceptable number of casualties on our patrols. Here's your next assignment.\031Is your task done yet, $N?",
[8741]="The Champion Returns\031The keeper awaits your return, $N. Take the green scepter shard to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time.\031Take the Green Scepter Shard to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris.",
[8742]="The Might of Kalimdor\031A thousand years has passed and just as it was fated, one stands before me. One who shall lead their people to a new age.$B$BThe Old God trembles, $N. Oh yes, it fears your faith. Shatter the prophecy of C'Thun.$B$BIt knows you come, champion - and with you comes the might of Kalimdor. You have only to let me know when you are prepared and I shall grant you The Scepter of the Shifting Sands.\031\031The Scepter of the Shifting Sands is whole once more, $N.$B$BIt must be you who uses the scepter. It must be you who heralds the next age of your people. You must wait for the armies of the Horde and the Alliance to arrive in Silithus before you may ring the Scarab Gong.",
[8743]="Bang a Gong!\031\031\031From the ground near the gong springs a special crystal. Perhaps favor from the Brood.\031The Scarab Gong looms ominously before you. Steel yourself, $N; for once the Scarab Gong is rung, the gates of Ahn'Qiraj will be opened.$B$BFrom the slackened maw of the beast can only come chaos and destruction. Defend your people!",
[8744]="A Carefully Wrapped Present\031\031\031The tag on this present reads:$B$BTo $N,$B$BMay your feast of Great-Winter be merry and bright!",
[8745]="Treasure of the Timeless One",
[8746]="Metzen the Reindeer\031DISASTER has struck!  Metzen the Reindeer has been kidnapped!$B$BMetzen is one of Great-father Winter's eight reindeer - and property of Smokywood Pastures.  We've received not one but TWO ransom letters from groups claiming to have Metzen.  With the holiday season well under way, we're strapped to the coin box here!  Please - find Metzen and return him to us!$B$BCheck out the ransom letters for clues, and sprinkle this reindeer dust on him - it will free him from any of his bonds!$B$BPlease, hurry!\031Find Metzen the Reindeer.  Use the notes provided to you for clues as to where he is being held.$B$BWhen you find Metzen, have the Pouch of Reindeer Dust in your possession so you can sprinkle some of the dust on him; this should free Metzen from his bonds of captivity.$B$BReturn the Pouch of Reindeer Dust to Kaymard Copperpinch in Orgrimmar once Metzen is freed.\031You did it!  Huzzah!$B$BMetzen flew back into Great-father Winter's stables - yes Metzen can really fly - just a little while ago!  The dust worked like a charm; I knew it would.  You've saved the Feast of Winter Veil as well as Smokywood Pastures from disaster.  Thank you, $N.$B$BListen... because of what you've done here, I want you to have this.  It's something VERY special; if you have a mount, I think you'll get a kick out of it.  Happy Winter Veil!\031$N!  Did you find him?  Were the notes in the satchel I gave you enough information to locate Metzen?  I hate to think of what those cruel thugs might do to him... but there's no way we can afford to pay such an exorbitant ransom!\031\031Find Metzen the Reindeer and rescue him",
[8747]="The Path of the Protector\031\031\031Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.$b$bThe signet ring of the protector will offer superior protection against the forces of evil.$b$bBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.",
[8748]="The Path of the Protector\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the protector!",
[8749]="The Path of the Protector\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the protector!",
[8750]="The Path of the Protector\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the protector!",
[8751]="The Protector of Kalimdor\031\031\031Rise, Protector of Kalimdor! Rise and be recognized!\031Never have I seen such tenacity! The Bronze Flight grants you one final enchantment. The Timeless One himself has requested it so!$b$bHand me your signet ring so that I may make the necessary adjustments.",
[8752]="The Path of the Conqueror\031\031\031Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.$b$bThe signet ring of the conqueror will greatly enhance your physical attacks.$b$bBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.",
[8753]="The Path of the Conqueror\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the conqueror!",
[8754]="The Path of the Conqueror\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the conqueror!",
[8755]="The Path of the Conqueror\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the conqueror!",
[8756]="The Qiraji Conqueror\031\031\031Rise, Qiraji Conqueror! Rise and be recognized!\031Never have I seen such tenacity! The Bronze Flight grants you one final enchantment. The Timeless One himself has requested it so!$b$bHand me your signet ring so that I may make the necessary adjustments.",
[8757]="The Path of the Invoker\031\031\031Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.$b$bThe signet ring of the invoker will greatly enhance your magical and natural abilities.$b$bBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.",
[8758]="The Path of the Invoker\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the invoker!",
[8759]="The Path of the Invoker\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the invoker!",
[8760]="The Path of the Invoker\031\031\031Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, $n. May you never stray from the path of the invoker!",
[8761]="The Grand Invoker\031\031\031Rise, Grand Invoker! Rise and be recognized!\031Never have I seen such tenacity! The Bronze Flight grants you one final enchantment. The Timeless One himself has requested it so!$b$bHand me your signet ring so that I may make the necessary adjustments.",
[8762]="Metzen the Reindeer\031DISASTER has struck!  Metzen the Reindeer has been kidnapped!$B$BMetzen is one of Greatfather Winter's eight reindeer - and property of Smokywood Pastures.  We've received not one but TWO ransom letters from groups claiming to have Metzen.  With the holiday season well under way, we're strapped to the coin box here!  Please - find Metzen and return him to us!$B$BCheck out the ransom letters for clues, and sprinkle this reindeer dust on him - it will free him from any of his bonds!$B$BPlease, hurry!\031Find Metzen the Reindeer.  Use the notes provided to you for clues as to where he is being held.$B$BWhen you find Metzen, have the Pouch of Reindeer Dust in your possession so you can sprinkle some of the dust on him; this should free Metzen from his bonds of captivity.$B$BReturn the Pouch of Reindeer Dust to Wulmort Jinglepocket in Ironforge once Metzen is freed.\031You did it!  Huzzah!$B$BMetzen flew back into Greatfather Winter's stables - yes Metzen can really fly - just a little while ago!  The dust worked like a charm; I knew it would.  You've saved the Feast of Winter Veil as well as Smokywood Pastures from disaster.  Thank you, $N.$B$BListen... because of what you've done here, I want you to have this.  It's something VERY special; if you have a mount, I think you'll get a kick out of it.  Happy Winter Veil!\031$N!  Were the notes in the satchel I gave you enough information to locate Metzen?  I hate to think of what those cruel thugs might do to him... but there's no way we can afford to pay such an exorbitant ransom!\031\031Find Metzen the Reindeer and rescue him",
[8763]="The Hero of the Day\031Listen... I'm not really supposed to be telling you this, but since you're the hero of the day and all...$B$BThere's fresh holly everywhere this time of the year, but it never lasts.  We've got a machine that preserves holly - it never goes bad!  We use it to spice up the holiday... and profits during the summer!$B$BI'll let you use the preserver, but only if you're a master cook.  You'll need some deeprock salt and two, three, oh let's say five gold.  It'll net you a nice batch that's yours to keep.\031Bring 1 Deeprock Salt and 5 gold coins to any Holly Preserver machine, upon which you will receive 5 Preserved Holly.",
[8764]="The Changing of Paths - Protector No More\031\031\031Be well, $n. If you change your mind, I shall be here to assist you.\031Champion, should you decide to walk another path, present me with your signet ring and a mountain of scarabs from our enemies in Ahn'Qiraj.",
[8765]="The Changing of Paths - Invoker No More\031\031\031Be well, $n. If you change your mind, I shall be here to assist you.\031Champion, should you decide to walk another path, present me with your signet ring and a mountain of scarabs from our enemies in Ahn'Qiraj.",
[8766]="The Changing of Paths - Conqueror No More\031\031\031Be well, $n. If you change your mind, I shall be here to assist you.\031Champion, should you decide to walk another path, present me with your signet ring and a mountain of scarabs from our enemies in Ahn'Qiraj.",
[8767]="A Gently Shaken Gift\031\031\031This present looks like it has been shaken a few times. The tag on it reads:$B$BTo a very special $R $C.",
[8768]="A Gaily Wrapped Present\031\031\031This festively-wrapped present has your name on it.$B$BWait, did it just move?",
[8769]="A Ticking Present\031\031\031Have a joyous Feast of Great-Winter from your friends at Smokeywood Pastures.",
[8770]="Target: Hive'Ashi Defenders\031As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations.  You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Ashi where your primary target will consist of Hive'Ashi defenders.$B$BReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.\031Slay 30 Hive'Ashi Defenders and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work, $N. Your diligence is as noteworthy as always.\031You have something to tell me, $C?",
[8771]="Target: Hive'Ashi Sandstalkers\031As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations.  You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Ashi where your primary target will consist of Hive'Ashi sandstalkers.$B$BReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.\031Slay 30 Hive'Ashi Sandstalkers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing II in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work, $N. Your part in the attack on Hive'Ashi has been noted.\031You have something to tell me, $C?",
[8772]="Target: Hive'Zora Waywatchers\031Reinforcements have been called on to join the assault on Hive'Zora.  You have been selected to target Hive'Zora waywatchers.  Report back to Commander Mar'alith after completing your task.\031Slay 30 Hive'Zora Waywatchers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing VI in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work, $N. Your part in the attack on Hive'Zora has been noted.\031You have something to tell me, $C?",
[8773]="Target: Hive'Zora Reavers\031Reinforcements have been called on to join the assault on Hive'Zora.  You have been selected to target Hive'Zora reavers.  Report back to Commander Mar'alith after completing your task.\031Slay 30 Hive'Zora Reavers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing IV in order to complete this quest.\031I've heard good things about your part in the Hive'Zora attack. Keep up the good work and victory will soon be ours.\031You have something to tell me, $C?",
[8774]="Target: Hive'Regal Ambushers\031As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations.  You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of the Hive'Regal ambushers.$B$BReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.\031Kill 30 Hive'Regal Ambushers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work, $N. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.\031You wish to tell me something, $N?",
[8775]="Target: Hive'Regal Spitfires\031As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations.  You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of the airborne Hive'Regal spitfires.$B$BReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.\031Kill 30 Hive'Regal Spitfires and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work, $N. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.\031You wish to tell me something, $N?",
[8776]="Target: Hive'Regal Slavemakers\031As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations.  You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of the Hive'Regal slavemakers.$B$BReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.\031Kill 30 Hive'Regal Slavemakers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work, $N. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.\031You wish to tell me something, $N?",
[8777]="Target: Hive'Regal Burrowers\031As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations.  You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of Hive'Regal burrowers.$B$BReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.\031Kill 30 Hive'Regal Burrowers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Combat Task Briefing XI in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work, $N. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.\031You wish to tell me something, $N?",
[8778]="The Ironforge Brigade Needs Explosives!\031The Ironforge Brigade has put in an unusual request for highly... volatile... components.  Gather them and bring them to Mr. Nozzlespring from the Ironforge Brigade.\031Bring 6 Oils of Immolation, 5 Goblin Rocket Fuel and 10 Dense Blasting Powder to Arcanist Nozzlespring near Hive'Zora in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IV in order to complete this quest.\031Ah, yes!  These will come in handy! Much obliged, $N!\031You have something for me, $N?",
[8779]="Scrying Materials\031Geologist Larksbane's studies have proven to be of tremendous value to our operations in Silithus.  She has recently requested scrying materials to be used in her research.$B$BPlease gather these materials and deliver them to her directly so that she may continue her research.\031Bring 1 Large Brilliant Shard, 1 Large Radiant Shard and 1 Huge Emerald to Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing V in order to complete this quest.",
[8780]="Armor Kits for the Field\031The Ironforge Brigade's supply of armor kits in the battlefield is running dangerously low.  Obtain a batch and deliver them to Janela Stouthammer at the Ironforge Brigade's outpost outside Hive'Zora.\031Bring 8 Rugged Armor Kits and 8 Heavy Armor Kits to Janela Stouthammer at the Ironforge Brigade Outpost near Hive'Zora in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VII in order to complete this quest.",
[8781]="Arms for the Field\031The Ironforge Brigade has been a worthy ally in our fight in Silithus.  Unfortunately, many of their supplies were lost on their way here.  Procure a batch of weapons and deliver them to Janela Stouthammer near Hive'Zora.\031Bring 2 Moonsteel Broadswords to Janela Stouthammer at the Ironforge Brigade Outpost outside of Hive'Zora.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VI in order to complete this quest.\031Oh, excellent! I won't have to hear complaints about dull blades anymore. Thank you, $N.\031You have something for me, $N?",
[8782]="Uniform Supplies\031The latest influx of volunteers has caused a shortage of uniforms.  Procure a batch of uniform materials and bring them to Windcaller Proudhorn.\031Bring 1 Mooncloth, 2 Bolts of Runecloth and 1 Ironweb Spider Silk to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.",
[8783]="Extraordinary Materials\031Vargus, Cenarion Hold's blacksmith, has requested enchanted materials to be used in the crafting of powerful weapons for our forces.  Obtain these and bring them directly to Vargus so that Cenarion Hold's troops may continue to be well equipped.\031Bring 2 Enchanted Thorium Bars and 2 Enchanted Leather to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.",
[8784]="Secrets of the Qiraji\031You have discovered an ancient Qiraji artifact! Perhaps one of the dragons near the entrance of the temple would have a use for this relic.\031Take the Ancient Qiraji Artifact to the dragons hiding near the entrance of the temple.\031An exceptional find, $N. Simply marvelous! This will definitely give us some insight into our enemy's twisted minds.\031You're glowing! I know what that means...",
[8785]="The Orgrimmar Legion Needs Mojo!\031The Orgrimmar Legion has put in a request for several unusual ingredients.  Given their current performance in Silithus, we'd like to comply with their request as soon as possible.  Gather the materials and bring them to the troll called Shai.\031Bring 6 Powerful Mojo, 6 Flasks of Big Mojo and 8 Oils of Immolation to Shadow Priestess Shai near Hive'Regal in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IV in order to complete this quest.\031Ah, yes. Just what I needed! I'll make a special concoction with this. The silithid won't like it one bit!\031Do you have my materials, $N?",
[8786]="Arms for the Field\031The Orgrimmar Legion has put in a request for additional weapons that we haven't been able to provide at the moment.  Obtain the weapons they've requested and bring them to Merok Longstride outside of Hive'Regal.\031Bring 3 Massive Iron Axes to Merok Longstride at the Orgrimmar Legion camp outside of Hive'Regal.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VI in order to complete this quest.\031Excellent work. We were in short supply of these, $N.\031You have something for me, $N?",
[8787]="Armor Kits for the Field\031The brave volunteers of the Orgrimmar Legion have arrived to Silithus to aid us in our cause.  Their supplies of armor kits were somehow lost in the trip.  Obtain a batch of armor kits and deliver them to Merok Longstride at the location of the Orgrimmar Legion camp.\031Bring 8 Rugged Armor Kits and 8 Heavy Armor Kits to Merok Longstride near Hive'Regal.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VII in order to complete this quest.\031Ah, yes... I will distribute these to the troops, $N. The Orgrimmar Legion thanks you!\031You have something for me, $N?",
[8788]="A Gently Shaken Gift\031\031\031This present looks like it has been shaken a few times. The tag on it reads:$B$BTo a very special $R $C.",
[8789]="Imperial Qiraji Armaments\031We have not sat idly by for a millennium, $N.$B$BWe have watched these beasts feast on their own when they have exhausted their utility. We have listened as they have plotted and schemed to destroy our world. And we have learned of their own internal treachery.$B$BWeaknesses exist and we know how to use those weaknesses to our advantage.$B$BFind and bring me their ceremonial armaments: Combined with the element created from the volatility of their own God, they will become a force of reckoning.\031Arygos in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj will create Elementium Infused Armaments for you should you bring him Imperial Qiraji Armaments and 3 Elementium Ore.\031Infused with Elementium, these weapons will cut through the Qiraji and their God with incredible ease.\031Seek out what I requested. You will become greater than the sum of your parts, champion.",
[8790]="Imperial Qiraji Regalia\031Arygos theorizes that the element which is born of conflicts between the Old Gods and their minions is also extremely deadly to them under the right conditions. I speak of Elementium, mortal.$B$BFind and bring me Imperial Qiraji Regalia and the toxic element and I shall infuse weapons of great power.\031Merithra of the Dream in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj will create Elementium Infused Armaments for you should you bring her Imperial Qiraji Regalia and 3 Elementium Ore.\031Use the item well, $N. Let them feel the pain that they so dearly wish to inflict upon others.\031You will strike them down and free us of these bonds.",
[8791]="The Fall of Ossirian\031A terrible menace has been laid to rest. The cruel Ossirian has been vanquished.$B$BThe denizens of Kalimdor would be relieved to know of this victory. Take Ossirian's head and present it to Commander Mar'alith of Cenarion Hold.\031Deliver the Head of Ossirian the Unscarred to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\031I offer you my highest commendation and your choice of an item of power, $N. You have done the people of Kalimdor a great service.\031Ah, $N, you have returned! And in one piece, I might add. What news do you bring from Ahn'Qiraj?",
[8792]="The Horde Needs Your Help!\031Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $N!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?\031Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.\031Throm'ka, $c! Good to see so many of the Horde, such as yourself, $n, coming out to lend your support in laying the groundwork for the upcoming Ahn'Qiraj War. The effort here will ensure that we are victorious against the Silithid and their evil masters hidden away inside Ahn'Qiraj.$b$bSo now that you are here, be sure to speak with the various collectors and offer your assistance in gathering those materials that you are suited to.",
[8793]="The Horde Needs Your Help!\031Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $N!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?\031Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.\031Throm'ka, $c! Good to see so many of the Horde, such as yourself, $n, coming out to lend your support in laying the groundwork for the upcoming Ahn'Qiraj War. The effort here will ensure that we are victorious against the Silithid and their evil masters hidden away inside Ahn'Qiraj.$b$bSo now that you are here, be sure to speak with the various collectors and offer your assistance in gathering those materials that you are suited to.",
[8794]="The Horde Needs Your Help!\031Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $N!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?\031Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.\031Throm'ka, $c! Good to see so many of the Horde, such as yourself, $n, coming out to lend your support in laying the groundwork for the upcoming Ahn'Qiraj War. The effort here will ensure that we are victorious against the Silithid and their evil masters hidden away inside Ahn'Qiraj.$b$bSo now that you are here, be sure to speak with the various collectors and offer your assistance in gathering those materials that you are suited to.",
[8795]="The Alliance Needs Your Help!\031Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $N!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?\031Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.",
[8796]="The Alliance Needs Your Help!\031Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $N!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?\031Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.",
[8797]="The Alliance Needs Your Help!\031Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $N!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?\031Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.",
[8798]="A Yeti of Your Own\031\031\031Say! You know what?! You're an engineer too! So, since you helped me teach my friends a lesson, I'm going to teach you how to make your very own mechanical yeti! Now the fun can go on forever and ever, and you can scare whoever you want! Provided that you can scare up the components to make it that is. $B$BWhat do you say, $N? Do you want to learn the secret to making a mechanical yeti?",
[8799]="The Hero of the Day\031Listen... I'm not really supposed to be telling you this, but since you're the hero of the day and all...$B$BThere's fresh holly everywhere this time of the year, but it never lasts.  We've got a machine that preserves holly - it never goes bad!  We use it to spice up the holiday... and profits during the summer!$B$BI'll let you use the preserver, but only if you're a master cook.  You'll need some deeprock salt and two, three, oh let's say five gold.  It'll net you a nice batch that's yours to keep.\031Bring 1 Deeprock Salt and 5 gold coins to the Holly Preserver machine, upon which you will receive 5 Preserved Holly.",
[8800]="Cenarion Battlegear\031As you complete the tasks you're assigned in the war you'll want to talk to Vargus, the blacksmith.  Show him any badges you've earned along the way. He'll provide you with gear to match your level of commitment to our cause.\031Talk to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\031Kaldon sent you? Very well, let's see what we can do for you.",
[8801]="C'Thun's Legacy\031The walls of Ahn'Qiraj tremble. A force of evil, older than the world itself, has been destroyed.$B$BAs you look at the remnants of the colossal abomination your heart nearly freezes. Even in death you can feel the legacy of C'Thun's evil around you.$B$BYou have done what was thought to be impossible.$B$BYou grab at an eye stalk of the fiend, stowing it safely in your pack.$B$BTake the Eye of C'Thun to the dragons in the next chamber.\031Take the Eye of C'Thun to Caelastrasz in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj.\031We will leave this place on our own, Lady $N - once we are certain that the evil within has been wholly destroyed. Your journey of legend is almost at an end.\031Lady $N, you have freed us of its grasp.",
[8802]="The Savior of Kalimdor\031To the Caverns of Time you go, $G Lord:Lady; $N. Anachronos awaits your return. Give him the eye of C'Thun as he will undoubtedly wish to place it in his master's collection.\031Take the Eye of C'Thun to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time.\031The Master has left these for you, champion. From the timeless cache: A collection of artifacts spanning thousands of years - the choice is yours.\031Lord $N! It is over...",
[8803]="A Festive Gift\031\031\031The note on this present reads:$B$BTo $N,$B$BIn hoping this will help you spread warm tidings and holiday cheer to all of Azeroth.$B$BFrom Greatfather Winter",
[8804]="Desert Survival Kits\031With the arrival of fresh recruits to Cenarion Hold comes the problem of keeping them alive in the desert.  Dehydration as well as numerous poisonous creatures present a serious threat to inexperienced volunteers.  Gather the supplies necessary for a desert survival kit and bring them to Calandrath in Cenarion Hold.\031Bring 4 Globes of Water, 4 Powerful Anti-Venom and 4 Smoked Desert Dumplings to Calandrath at the inn in Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.",
[8805]="Boots for the Guard\031The mounted division of the Cenarion Hold guard is in short supply of ornate mithril boots.  Procure a batch and deliver them immediately to Captain Vish Kozus in Cenarion Hold.\031Bring 3 Ornate Mithril Boots to Vish Kozus, Captain of the Guard at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing II in order to complete this quest.",
[8806]="Grinding Stones for the Guard\031The Cenarion Hold guard is in short supply of grinding stones.  Procure a batch and deliver them immediately to Captain Vish Kozus in Cenarion Hold.\031Bring 10 Dense Grinding Stones, 10 Solid Grinding Stones and 10 Heavy Grinding Stones to Vish Kozus, Captain of the Guard at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing III in order to complete this quest.",
[8807]="Scrying Materials\031Geologist Larksbane's studies have proven to be of tremendous value to our operations in Silithus.  She has recently requested scrying materials to be used in her research.$B$BPlease gather these materials and deliver them to her directly so that she may continue her research.\031Bring 1 Large Brilliant Shard, 1 Large Radiant Shard and 1 Huge Emerald to Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing V in order to complete this quest.",
[8808]="Uniform Supplies\031The latest influx of volunteers has caused a shortage of uniforms.  Procure a batch of uniform materials and bring them to Windcaller Proudhorn.\031Bring 1 Mooncloth, 2 Bolts of Runecloth and 1 Ironweb Spider Silk to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.",
[8809]="Extraordinary Materials\031Vargus, Cenarion Hold's blacksmith, has requested enchanted materials to be used in the crafting of powerful weapons for our forces.  Obtain these and bring them directly to Vargus so that Cenarion Hold's troops may continue to be well equipped.\031Bring 2 Enchanted Thorium Bars and 2 Enchanted Leather to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.",
[8810]="Bandages for the Field\031Our supply of bandages in the battlefield is running dangerously low after the recent casualties we have incurred.  Obtain a batch of first-aid supplies and deliver them to Windcaller Proudhorn in Cenarion Hold.\031Bring 30 Heavy Runecloth Bandages, 30 Heavy Silk Bandages and 30 Heavy Mageweave Bandages to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\031\031You have something for me, $N?$b$b",
[8811]="One Commendation Signet\031\031\031Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, $C.$B$BIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.\031For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Stormwind.$B$BPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.$B$BWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.",
